# Copy this file to .env and fill in your own values. Never commit .env.
# These three values end up inside the public JavaScript bundle. That is normal for EmailJS:
# the public key is designed to be public. Protect it with the domain allow-list and
# rate limits in your EmailJS dashboard (see README, Security section).
# Do NOT put an EmailJS private key or access token here.
